Slipstream is designed for serious writing and distraction-free reading. Standard prose notes are constrained to an optimal reading measure of `72ch` (`840px`), preventing excessive line lengths that cause eye fatigue.

---

! 1. The Ergonomic Reading Column

Long lines on wide desktop monitors make reading difficult because the reader's eye must track a great distance to find the beginning of the next line. Typographic research suggests that `65ch` to `75ch` is optimal for continuous prose.

In Slipstream:
* Standard notes stay centered at `var(--mn-reading-width, 840px)`.
* Full-bleed dashboards and data tables break out to `var(--mn-wide-width, 1120px)` using the `Wide` tag or `page-width: wide` field.
* Reading width can be customized anytime in [[$:/plugins/mblackman/slipstream/settings]].

---

! 2. Live Heading Outline Extraction

Any headings you write in your document are automatically extracted into a clickable, hierarchical table of contents:

* Look at the **Right Context Inspector** on desktop (or tap `•••` on mobile).
* Switch to the **Outline** tab.
* Headings (`!`, `!!`, `!!!`) are rendered dynamically as links. Clicking any heading jumps directly to that section.

---

! 3. Native Design Tokens & Palette Independence

Slipstream never hardcodes palette colors in its core components. Instead, it relies on TiddlyWiki v5.4.0+ native palette variables:

| !Variable | !Role |
| `--tpc-page-background` | Background behind the story river and navigation rails |
| `--tpc-background` | Background for tiddler cards, sheets, and popups |
| `--tpc-foreground` | Primary text color |
| `--tpc-primary` | Accent color for active items, buttons, and links |
| `--tpc-muted-foreground` | Secondary subtitles, timestamps, and labels |

When you switch between light, dark, Solarized, or Nord palettes in [[$:/ControlPanel]], Slipstream updates instantly without needing theme overrides.

---

! 4. Typography Elements

Standard wikitext formatting works seamlessly in Slipstream:

* ''Bold'' (`''bold''`) and //Italic// (`//italic//`)
* `Inline code` (`` `code` ``) and code blocks (```` ```javascript ````)
* Blockquotes (`> quote text`) with accent borders
* Tables with header highlighting and zebra striping
